			"hadithnumber": 3823,
			"arabicnumber": 3823,
			"text": "Narrated AbuSa'id al-Khudri: The garlic and onions were mentioned before the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He was told: The most severe of them is garlic. Would you make it unlawful? The Prophet (ﷺ) said: Eat it, and he who eats it should not come near this mosque until its odour goes away",
